  "body": "Stacked on #4251. This PR contains the commits of #4251. Merge #4251 first; then this PR takes `git merge origin/main` and a new gate. Do not merge this PR before #4251.\n\n## What changed\n\nThird slice of #3919. The built-in holder library gets:\n\n- **SK50** (DIN 69871 / DIN ISO 7388-1 size 50): Ø69.85 gauge, Ø97.5 flange, 3.2 standoff, 15.9 flange. It has ER16-ER50 collet chucks and every Weldon bore (6-20 mm, 1/4-3/4 in). The default gauge length is 100. It is in `crates/tools/src/holder_library_din.rs`, after SK40.\n- **ER50** (Ø5-34 collets, Ø78 M64×2 nut, drawn 40 long) in the one ER table. It is on BT40, CAT40, SK40, BT50, CAT50 and SK50, with a default gauge length of 100. There is no standalone ER50 chuck.\n- **SK50 is a spindle mount**: `SPINDLE_MOUNTS` has 14 names, with SK50 after SK40. The app test `every_library_taper_is_a_spindle_mount` keeps the list equal to the library.\n\nThe ER50 nut is wider than a 40-taper flange. The body is drawn at the nut width up to the flange front, with no flare. The flange steps in from it, so the outline is never smaller than the steel.\n\nEach number and its source is in `docs/decisions/3919-standard-holders-3.md`.\n\nLeft out, with the reasons in the decision file:\n- SK50 shrink-fit: the slice-2 shrink-fit tables have no SK50 table.\n- TG75 / TG100: TG is a trade system, and we found no standard table.\n- Morse MT2-MT5: DIN 228 fixes only the taper. The collar below the spindle face has no standard table.\n- NMTB 30 / 40: we found no published flange table.\n- Hydraulic and milling chucks: each maker designs its own body.\n- A standalone ER50 chuck.\n- SF32: it waits for the owner's measurements.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `holder_library::din::sk50_tests::*` (new file `crates/tools/src/holder_library_sk50_tests.rs`):\n  - `sk50_and_er50_match_the_recorded_table`\n  - `the_sk50_and_er50_entries_are_listed`\n  - `the_sk50_er50_outline_is_the_table`\n  - `a_bt40_er50_body_wider_than_its_flange_is_drawn_whole`\n  - `an_er50_chuck_takes_its_collet_range`\n- These tests are updated for the new rows: `the_tapers_and_nuts_match_the_recorded_table`, `the_din_entries_are_listed`, `the_50_taper_entries_are_listed`, `the_shrink_entries_are_listed` (SK50 has no shrink-fit entry), `the_picker_shows_one_weldon_row_for_each_taper` and `the_new_library_tapers_are_spindle_mounts` (post).\n\n## Gate results (head 5ea83cb93, base #4251 head 9921f2961)\n\nwinbuild (Windows, 5 jobs):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-tools --lib`: pass, 219 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib`: pass, 161 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass, no warnings.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test holder_library --test machine_default_holder --test holder_reference`: pass, 12 + 7 + 14 passed, 0 failed.\n\nMac:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 9921f2961`: pass, 96 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (13.9 min). This includes the tools lib, the post build and suites, and the app suites `machine_default_holder` and `mcp_holder`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base 9921f2961`: pass, 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (14.2 min).\n\nNot exercised: the light lane and the heavy lanes. No toolpath and no post output changed, so the example catalog suites do not apply. The UI was not started.\n\nChangelog: The holder library has SK50 holders (ER16-ER50, Weldon) and ER50 collet chucks on the BT40, CAT40, SK40, BT50, CAT50 and SK50 tapers. SK50 is a spindle mount for machine files.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #3919\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork. No image is in the PR branch. \"Before\" is `main`. \"After\" is this head. The shrink-fit rows are in #4251, not in this PR: see its screenshots at https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/4251 (images at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4251/after-holder-picker.png and https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4251/after-holders-page.png).\n\nHolder picker, before: the list has no SK50 row and no ER50 row.\n\n![before: holder picker](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/before-holder-picker-er50.png)\n\nHolder picker, after: the list has SK50 ER16 to SK50 ER50 and SK50 Weldon.\n\n![after: holder picker, SK50 rows](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/after-holder-picker-er50.png)\n\nHolder picker, after: a pick of SK50 ER50 shows its flange, nut and collet range.\n\n![after: SK50 ER50 picked](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/after-holder-picked-sk50-er50.png)\n\nHolders page filtered to \"SK50\", before: the list is empty.\n\n![before: Holders page, SK50](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/before-holders-page-sk50.png)\n\nHolders page filtered to \"SK50\", after: 17 rows, six ER collets and eleven Weldon rows.\n\n![after: Holders page, SK50](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/after-holders-page-sk50.png)\n\nHolders page filtered to \"ER50\", before: the list is empty.\n\n![before: Holders page, ER50](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/before-holders-page-er50.png)\n\nHolders page filtered to \"ER50\", after: BT40 ER50, CAT40 ER50, SK40 ER50, SK50 ER50, BT50 ER50 and CAT50 ER50.\n\n![after: Holders page, ER50](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4276/after-holders-page-er50.png)\n\n",
